    <!-- Guided tour and about -->
    <string name="tour_title_scope_business">Businesses and Projects</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_scope_business">Select and manage your business units and active projects. Each business\'s data is fully isolated — transactions, reports, and backups are all independent. Removing one business does not affect any other.</string>
    <string name="tour_title_scope_book">Plan vs Actual Ledgers</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_scope_book">Plan (budget/RAB) and Actual (cash on hand) books are strictly separated. Fill in the Plan as a cost and revenue simulation, record Actual during the business period, then compare both in Reports → Comparison tab to judge your planning accuracy.</string>
    <string name="tour_title_hero_summary">Financial Executive Summary</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_hero_summary">Monitor operating cash balance, net profit, cash flow, and outstanding receivables or payables in real time. If your balance looks negative but you still have money on hand, you likely haven\'t recorded your starting capital — enter \"Own Capital\" in the Records menu to fix the balance.</string>
    <string name="tour_title_nav_entry">Transaction Records Menu</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_nav_entry">Log cash income/expenses, credit sales/purchases, and inspect the complete transaction history in the Records List tab.</string>
    <string name="tour_title_nav_reports">Reports &amp; Feasibility Analysis</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_nav_reports">Access income statements, cash flow, and automated feasibility metrics: Break-even (BEP), Unit Cost (HPP), B/C Ratio, and PDF/Excel export.</string>
    <string name="tour_title_nav_more">Files &amp; Data Menu</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_nav_more">Import and export Excel workbooks (.xlsx), perform encrypted AES-256-GCM cloud backups to Google Drive, and manage account settings.</string>
    <string name="tour_title_scope">Business, Project, and Mode</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_scope">Choose the active business and project, and switch between Plan (projection) and Actual (real records).</string>
    <string name="tour_title_summary">Cash and Cost Summary</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_summary">Watch your working cash, profit or loss, and where the spending goes, updated as you record.</string>
    <string name="tour_title_nav">Main Navigation</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_nav">Use the bottom menu to record daily transactions, build the budget plan, and read the feasibility analysis (BEP and B/C ratio).</string>
    <string name="tour_title_cost_chart">Cost breakdown</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_cost_chart">Every expense is sorted automatically by your business accounts (such as Wages, Stock Purchases, Rent, Utilities, Delivery, Marketing, etc.). Keep an eye on your largest cost drivers to optimize operational spending.</string>
    <string name="tour_entry_tabs_title">New record or history</string>
    <string name="tour_entry_tabs_desc">The left tab records a new transaction, the right one lists everything already entered. The number on the right tab is how many records exist for the project and book you are working in.</string>
    <string name="tour_entry_kinds_title">Choose the kind of transaction</string>
    <string name="tour_entry_kinds_desc">Money in and Money out cover everyday cash. Tap \"Other kinds\" for own capital, loans, tool purchases, and credit sales or purchases that create receivables and payables. Each kind automatically generates the correct journal: Money In = debit Cash + credit Revenue, Credit Purchase = debit Expense + credit Payable. Fill in volume and unit (pcs, kg, units, portions) when you want the unit price worked out for you.</string>
    <string name="tour_entry_history_title">History and corrections</string>
    <string name="tour_entry_history_desc">Any record can be reversed with a reversing journal entry: the amount is neutralised but the trail stays, so the books remain auditable. There is also a \"Delete\" option that permanently removes the record — use it only when the entry was genuinely entered in error and no correction trail is needed.</string>
    <string name="tour_reports_tabs_title">Three points of view</string>
    <string name="tour_reports_tabs_desc">Financials answers \"what did I make\", Feasibility answers \"is this worth continuing\", and Comparison answers \"how far did actual drift from plan\".</string>
    <string name="tour_reports_profit_title">Profit and cash flow</string>
    <string name="tour_reports_profit_desc">Net profit = operating income − operating cost. It is accrual-based: a credit sale counts as income before the money arrives. Operating cash flow counts only money that actually moved, so the two differing is normal, not an error.</string>
    <string name="tour_reports_feasibility_title">Break-even, cost per unit, B/C ratio</string>
    <string name="tour_reports_feasibility_desc">Break-even rupiah: the minimum turnover that avoids a loss. Break-even volume: the minimum sales/production volume to cover every cost. Cost per unit (COGS/HPP): what one unit costs you to produce or acquire — selling below it loses money. B/C ratio: revenue divided by cost; above 1 the business pays, below 1 the costs exceed the income. Fill in the assumptions (target quantity and selling price) to make all four appear. These four metrics help you decide whether your venture is sustainable and profitable.</string>
